WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:07.299
Shanks vs Luffy, Usopp vs Loki and Blackbeard
waiting for his turn to collect the strongest

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:09.380
mythical Zoan fruit.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:14.490
Even though Wano is already one of my favourite
arcs in all of One Piece, there has been no

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:21.230
other arc I have been as excited for and as
anxious about as the legendary kingdom of

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.050
the mighty giants: Elbaf.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:27.980
Because I'm convinced that it's not only gonna
be the Straw Hat's next destination after

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:33.280
Wano, but also the most important arc for
the endgame of One Piece after Laugh Tale

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.280
itself.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.640
And today, I want to try and predict as well
as I can, how all these epic events might

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:47.350
unfold themselves during the Elbaf arc.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:56.890
Hi, my name is Manu and even though, as someone
so obsessed with Japanese culture that I packed

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:02.480
my stuff and moved to Tokyo, I have been enjoying
the ongoing Japan-inspired Wano Kuni arc a

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.470
lot, -- it has been going on for a while now.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:15.150
To be precise, it started with chapter 909,
back in July of 2018, which was 4 YEARS AGO!

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.270
I wasn't even thinking about doing Youtube
then.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:23.060
So as much as I'm enjoying, what I can just
hope to be the actual climax of this arc at

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:28.869
the moment, I found it increadibly refreshing
to look ahead and think about what the future

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:30.509
of one piece will bring.

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:36.310
And in that, hopefully not all-too distant
future, I see a rocky island in the shadow

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:47.880
of a gigantic tree, inhabited by the most
powerful mythical beings imaginable.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.490
Cue epic viking music.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:56.130
Instead of Japanese mythology, sakura trees
and samurai, we'll have Nordic mythology,

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.469
snowy mountain peaks and vikings.

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:04.579
And just so you know, next to Japan of course,
Norway has been my favorite place I’ve ever

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:05.579
lived.

00:02:05.579 --> 00:02:10.080
And I honestly think Elbaf's layout will be
heavily inspired by that.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:16.220
With icy winds, long nights and banquets with
a lot of alcohol, the most stunning place

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:22.459
I have ever laid eyes on are theso-called
loften islands in the far north of Norway.

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:27.580
Please tell me that this doesn’t look exactly
like what we've seen of Elbaf's coastline

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.620
so far.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:34.700
If there is one place on earth I recommend
you just have to see, it's this one.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:41.980
Okay, so now that we have set the right mood,
how likely is it that we will even go to elbaf.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.620
After all, it hasn't been officially confirmed
at all if we're actually gonna go there and

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:52.560
author Eiichiro Oda has to keep pushing back
his goal for finishing One Piece as is.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:58.230
So the only way for an Elbaf arc to exist
is if it heavily contributes to the climax

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:04.330
of the series, pushes the story and development
further and has a clear connection to Wano.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:10.180
And for full disclosure, it is of course absolutely
possible, that Elbaf will be skipped or just

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.330
be referenced in passing by Oda.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:17.760
That being said, there is a really good reason,
why me and large parts of the fandom find

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:24.879
that possibility unlikely and basically take
a visit to Elbaf for granted: It has been

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:32.280
foreshadowed as far back as chapter 115, when
the straw hats arrived on little garden, where

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:41.060
they met the giants Dory and Broggy.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:42.060
[]

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:47.270
There are so many important character arcs,
that are all bound to culminate into Elbaf.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:50.239
At the center of it all is undoubtedly Usopp.

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:55.800
I have just recently made a full video on
Usopp's character development and why Elbaf

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.710
will be his big arc.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:02.239
So if you haven't seen it already, I strongly
recommend you check that one out after.

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:07.700
But all you have to know for now, is that
Usopp has been forging friendships with the

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:12.550
Giants of Elbaf trough-out the story, where
he has gained their respect and loyalty, and

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:18.660
on more than one occasion, has promised to
go to Elbaf one day to become a brave warrior

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:27.180
of the sea like his giant friends.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.820
And don’t worry, I'll be telling you what
I believe will happen with Usopp in just a

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:32.820
bit.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:37.720
The other character that has major connections
to the giants is none other than the Emperess

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:43.670
herself, Big Mom, who not only grew up on
Elbaf, but who also has a crazy obsession

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:49.430
with integrating the giants into her ideal
world, even though the giants despise her

00:04:49.430 --> 00:05:00.500
for her actions as a child.[] 
But surprisingly enough, Big Mom isn't the

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.250
only emperor with ties to this island.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:09.470
In my character analysis on Shanks, I explored
the strong ties Shanks has to nordic mythology.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:14.640
In fact, not only does he sail on a viking
ship, but his entire character seems to be

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.130
inspired by the nordic god tyr.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:22.970
In that video, I explore the idea, that Elbaf
might in fact be under the protection of the

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:27.700
red hair pirates and since Wano will be the
arc, where Luffy will finally rise into the

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:33.090
ranks of the Yonko, it is about time that
he met his mentor again, now that he has become

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:37.520
the great pirate Shanks wanted him to be.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:45.920
[shanks after WCI] Aside from these character
arcs, it seems like ELbaf might be home to

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:51.380
the father tree Adam from which's wood the
thousand sunny was made . It has been speculated

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:56.150
that this tree might be the main entrance
to the sky islands, but no matter what it

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:02.290
will turn out to be, it will play some important
role in the lore of the story, should it actually

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.530
be there.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:09.120
If you watch carefully, in the next clip you
can see something that looks suspiciously

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.470
like a giant tree trunk in the back.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:14.470
[]

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:21.510
And this might be a bit of a stupid argument,
but if Oda had planned to skip going to Elbaf

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:26.600
altogether, he surely would have shown it
off to us in all its glory instead of shrouding

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:30.480
it in so much mystery and barely giving us
a glimpse of its shoreline.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:36.370
Oh and, we have this pretty telling cover
spread of the straw hats as vikings.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:40.770
So, with all that being said, I want to now
share with you my time-line of all the things

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:45.530
that could and in my opinion should happen
during the Elbaf arc.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:49.811
And while I base all of this as well on everything
that has been foreshadowed in the story, keep

00:06:49.811 --> 00:06:52.730
in mind, that I could be completley wrong.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:58.220
That being said, I do belive there is a pretty
good chance a good chunk of this will happen

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.990
in some way or form.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:04.900
So, After a long and gruesome battle, we finally
depart Wano.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:10.470
Luffy has defeated Kaido and established himself
as an emperor, and the borders of Wano have

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:12.570
finally been opened.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:17.500
With the monster trio incapable of doing anything
for a while after their big fights, it was

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:22.120
the straw hat grand fleet that had come to
their help, when it looked like both Luffy

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.070
and Kaido were about to be disposed off.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.800
This could either be by the world government
or Blackbeard.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.880
This way the crew is saved and Wano is able
to start rebuilding itself.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:39.260
Now, While the grand fleet had sworn their
loyalty to luffy, most of them are actually

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:42.310
loyal to Usopp as well.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:51.870
And with the big 3 knocked out for a while,
Usopp finds himself in command by accident

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:58.800
as substitute captain, starting off his arc
by fulfilling two of his lies: Leading thousands

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:00.900
of men and being a captain.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:12.810
However, since it was by accident, Usopp will
probably do a bad job of leading at first.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:17.410
After arriving on Elbaf, I can see the first
half of the arc focusing on the culture of

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:21.000
the giants and the issues of their nation.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:28.310
During Whole Cake island, Prince Loki seems
to have been set up as the main villain here.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:36.950
Loki, who we know from nordic mythology as
a trickster and manipulator, has somehow managed

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:42.460
to take control of the giants, possibly getting
rid of Dory and Broggy and has even convinced

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:47.320
them to forget their hatred of Big Mom and
made them allow him to marry Lola, though

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:49.450
she refused in the end.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:53.550
Now Loki is confronted by another trickster
and manipulator.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:59.440
Usopp, who has gained respect and loyalty
among many of the elbaf giants.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:04.640
Both of them might be quite similar in terms
of their personality, but while Usopp values

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:10.330
bravery and wants to be like the giants, Loki
mostly values himself.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:16.050
At this point it would be a waste, if Oda
didn't give Usopp a Mjolnir-like hammer, to

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:20.380
parallel Thor and Loki.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:24.180
[usopp hammer attacks]

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:30.020
Soon, Usopp tries to expose Loki's trickery,
possibly triggered by the arrival of Big Mom,

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:36.160
siding with Loki and maybe Lola, who Big Mom
will try to marry off once again.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:42.240
Usopp counts on the other straw hats to stop
Loki, which doesn't happen with Luffy, Zoro

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:44.680
and Sanji out of the game.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:50.170
So, finally, after seeing the giants suffer
and being begged by Nami to help Lola, he

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:56.440
ends up doing the right thing, taking matters
into his own hands and challenging Loki to

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.440
a duel.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:02.879
Now we have the classic theme of David with
his slingshot vs. the giant Goliath.

00:10:02.879 --> 00:10:08.220
The fight itself goes on just as you imagine:
Usopp will try using tricks, hammers, dials,

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:15.050
and even Observation Haki against Loki, but
despite a few minor successes, nothing really

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.050
works.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.460
He’s a giant, after all.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:22.230
Finally, Loki hurts Usopp so badly, that he
almost wins the fight.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:26.930
And in combination with Usopp’s previous
failure as a leader, this pushes him into

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.070
despair.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:32.780
This is where Usopp's conquerors Haki kicks
in, something that I discussed in detail in

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:40.310
the previous video.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:46.170
Using Conqueror’s Haki, Usopp knocks down
the Giant Prince of Elbaf, terrifying all

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:51.870
those watching, and earning the respect of
the Giants, who will call him ‘a Brave Warrior

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:52.870
of the Sea’.

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:59.060
A tale so epic, that it’s only worthy of
such a legendary figure as God Usopp.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:03.420
And thus another lie has come true, Usopp
having conquerors haki.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:08.300
Not only does he liberate the giants of Elbaf,
but he also gains the right to lead the grand

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:15.570
fleet and the giants, numbering 8000 men into
battle behind Luffy at the end of the story.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:20.400
And most importantyl he convices everyone
to subscribe to this channel.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.900
A true legend.

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:24.700
This is where the second half of the arc begins.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:29.740
Luffy and the others just got back on their
in time feet to witness Usopp's victory.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:32.920
Amid the celebrations, a ship arrives at the
harbour.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:34.580
A viking ship.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:39.320
Luffy turns around and sees Shanks and his
men walking towards them.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:45.470
Luffy starts grinning and runs towards shanks,
shouting and waving, but the emperor just

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:51.380
pulls out his sword with a stern face and
prepares to attack Luffy.

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:56.750
Confused by this, Luffy keeps running and
only in the last moment reacts to Shank's

00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:01.410
attack.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:06.740
The sky splits above elbaf- and suddenly Shanks
smiles.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:11.880
He puts his arm around Luffy and congratulates
him on his accomplishments in Wano.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:16.910
As it turns out, he is the protector of Elbaf
and thanks Usopp for taking care of things

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.600
in his stead.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:24.360
That night the straw hats and red hair pirates
have their first big banquet together, Luffy

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.830
and Shanks now on one level with each other.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:30.870
During the festivities, a dark shape walks
into town.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:34.860
As he reaches the fires, we can see his face.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:41.550
[mihawk arrives on shanks island] It's Mihawk,
who has sought out his old rival after the

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:46.730
abandonment of the warlord system together
with Perona, who bring news, that Blackbeard

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:53.180
is on his way to Elbaf and will arrive in
a few days.

00:12:53.180 --> 00:13:01.690
As if this news didn't matter at all, Shanks
invites Mihawk to drink and while persona

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:06.810
reunites with Zoro, he reveals that he is
in possession of the last road poneglyph and

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:12.380
challenges Luffy to a davie back fight for
it, to test his strength and that of his crew.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:17.900
We then get a number of contests between the
straw hats and the red hair pirates, where

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:23.320
each of them shows off their skills and proves
their worth, including the long-awaited match

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.570
between Zoro and Mihawk.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:32.700
After teaching everyone new ticks and techniques,
Shanks and the others push luffy to leave

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.400
the island before Blackbeard arrive.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:40.761
In order to give Luffy a head-start for Laugh
Tale, but also as the Patreon of Elbaf, he

00:13:40.761 --> 00:13:44.850
will stay and face the man who gave him his
scar.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:49.340
Probably things will turn out quite differently,
but I hope you enjoyed this version of events

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:50.340
nonetheless.

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:54.500
You should click here if you want to learn
more about Usopp's role in Elbaf and why he

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.230
might unlock conquerors haki.

